    <DataNode elementId="AT1G79460-MONOMER" textLabel="ent-kaurene synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SAK2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana ga2-1&lt;/i&gt; mutant is a non-germinating, extreme dwarf whose mutant phenotypes is similar to that observed for the strong &lt;i&gt;ga1&lt;/i&gt; alleles and can be restored by exogenous application of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene |CITS:[9536043]|. Cell-free preparations from &lt;i&gt;ga2&lt;/i&gt; mutant siliques lack &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene synthase activity. The functional study of the &lt;i&gt;KS1&lt;/i&gt; gene (also known as &lt;i&gt;GA2&lt;/i&gt;) demonstrated that the protein (AtKS1) encoded by this gene has &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene synthase B activity, which is responsible for the conversion of copalyl diphosphate (CPP) into &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene |CITS:[9536043]|. The gene was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; where it was shown to convert a significant amount of CPP into &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene |CITS:[9536043]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G79460-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G79460.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SAK2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAD30231" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtKS" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="At1g79460" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="KS" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="GA2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-4260" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G79460.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G79460" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="74." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="74." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11722763" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_9536043" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12805613" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G32440-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G32440-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9C5Y2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis KAO2&lt;/i&gt; gene was expressed in yeast and shown to encode for an enzyme (KAO, &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurenoic acid oxidase) catalyzing the three steps of the gibberellin biosynthesis pathway from &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurenoic acid (KA) to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[11172076]|. Those three steps, involving the sequential triple hydroxylation at carbon positions C-7 and C-6, go as follows: KA to &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid (7OH-KA) (step1) to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde (step2) to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; (step3). KAO2, heterologously expressed in yeast was shown to convert KA to 7OH-KA and GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;; GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde was not detected |CITS:[11172076]|. This C-7 oxidase belongs to the superfamily of CYP88A cytochrome P450s. The enzyme has not been purified to homogeneity for kinetic studies.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G32440-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G32440.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_180803" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9C5Y2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP88A4" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33277, RXN-11954, RXN-11953, RXN-11935" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G32440.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G32440" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Species" value="ARA" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11172076" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G05160-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G05160-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O23051" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis KAO1&lt;/i&gt; gene was expressed in yeast and shown to encode for an enzyme (KAO, &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurenoic acid oxidase) catalyzing the three steps of the gibberellin biosynthesis pathway from &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[11172076]|. Those three steps, involving the sequential triple hydroxylation at carbon positions C-7 and C-6, go as follows: KA to &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid (7OH-KA) (step1) to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde (step2) to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; (step3). KAO1, heterologously expressed in yeast was shown to convert KA to 7OH-KA and GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;; GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde was not detected but, when used as a substrate, was converted to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[11172076]|. This C-7 enzyme belongs to the superfamily of CYP88A cytochrome P450s. The enzyme has not been purified to homogeneity for kinetic studies.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G05160-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G05160.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="O23051" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O23051" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP88A3" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33087, RXN-11951, RXN-11931, RXN-11936" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
