      <Comment source="BioCyc">Requires cytochrome &lt;i&gt;P&lt;/i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;450&lt;/sub&gt;. Catalyses three successive oxidations of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurenoic acid. The second step includes a ring-B contraction giving the gibbane skeleton. In pumpkin (&lt;i&gt;Cucurbita maxima&lt;/i&gt;) &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-6&amp;alpha;,7&amp;alpha;-dihydroxykaur-16-en-19-oate is also formed.</Comment>
