      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">NIL The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure. The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure. The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure. The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure. The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure. The conversion of &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-7&amp;alpha;-hydroxy kaurenoic acid to GA&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt;-aldehyde involves the contraction of ring B from six C atoms to five, thereby transforming the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurane carbon skeleton to the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-gibberellane structure.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="RXN1F-160" />
